Hi Marc,

As I said earlier all your replies really helped me out in my analysis. I have one more question though.

So instead of using ranef function for latent distribution, I have written below mentioned code.

> #avg_fms is fitList of all candidate models
> #model-averaged prediction
> #since models were of type trend, there is no omega
> #Abundance is given by N[t+1]=N[t]*gamma
> lambda<-predict(avg_fms, type="lambda")[,1] #line 1 gives 101 values in length
> gamma<-predict(avg_fms,type="gamma") #line 2 gives 404 values in length and they are not constant values
> N<-matrix(NA, length(lambda),4)
> N[,1]<-lambda
> N[,2]<-lambda*gamma
> N[,3]<-N[,2]*gamma
> N[,4]<-N[,3]*gamma
> N.total<-colSums(N)
The problem I am getting is, my data has 101 rows, so does my lambda (line1) but I get 404 different values of gamma. So my lambda and gamma differ in lengths and so I can't calculate abundance in next years.

Can you please tell me why this is happening and how to rectify this? This is one way that I could think of for calculating latent distribution.

Thanks,
Leo
